@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@
+# Reusable arithmetic graph invocation plans
+
+The development-only `runner_graph_plans.py` lowers syntax to JSON-compatible invocation
+plans. It never evaluates operand results or emits FFN weights. The native entrypoint
+should accept a bound Program packet, not Python source. Load reusable graphs for widths
+1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 and 62 at boot; requests select them and bind raw tensor Values.
+
+## Native packet and named plans
+
+The codec follows `tools/runner-graph-native.md` exactly. An inline packet is
+`{"version":1,"values":["12","-3"],"ops":[{"op":"add","a":0,"b":1,"width":4}],"result":2}`.
+References index values first, then every operation output in append order. Multi-output
+calls use `args` and `outputs:2`. The live path uses only
+`{"version":1,"plan":"add-4","values":["12","-3"]}`. There are no request-side ops,
+weights, dimensions, syntax parsing, or compilation on this path.
+
+`binary_plan(op,width,exponent=None)` returns `{name,inputs,literals,ops,result}` for
+the manifest's `plans` list. References index requested inputs first, then built-in
+`literals`, then outputs. `plan_id` and `binary_request(source)` select the exact ID:
+`add-N`, `sub-N`, `mul-N`, `div-N`, `mod-N`, or `pow-E-62` for exponent E in 0..999.
+`binary_request` chooses buckets from literal lengths, reserves one extra digit for
+add/sub and the sum of input digit lengths for mul, and caps at 62. Powers share
+width-62 mul graphs across all exponent schedules. Their single input is the base;
+the exponent is plan selection metadata. The built-in pools contain only zero/one.
+Exponent zero checks base error through mul-by-zero and add-one FFNs.
+
+`loop_plan(shape,bound,width=62)` names plans `loop-SHAPE-BOUND-WIDTH`. Shapes are
+`sum` (range 0..bound), `squares`, `factorial` (1..bound), `fib` and `list_sum`.
+Bounds are 0..128. All except `list_sum` take zero request inputs and bind offline
+seed/index literals; `list_sum` takes bound request operands. Fibonacci implements
+simultaneous tuple assignment. `plan_catalog()` emits the complete default catalog.
+
+## Native tensor transport
+
+The native helper's `bind` Op supports both required tensor transfers. No new opcode
+or arbitrary dimensions are needed. To extract A's digit i into digit zero:
+`{"op":"bind","copies":[{"ref":A,"from":i,"to":0,"digits":1}],"flags":A}`.
+Its source sign is irrelevant to divstep, which reads only digit/error lanes.
+
+To insert divstep output D's quotient digit into Q at position i:
+`{"op":"bind","copies":[{"ref":Q,"from":0,"to":0,"digits":N},{"ref":D,"from":0,"to":i,"digits":1}],"flags":D}`.
+D's sign is zero and its sticky error includes every preceding division step.
+Copies execute in order, preserve template reference columns at invocation, and do
+no numeric decoding. A width-N division plan has 2N binds and N divstep calls followed
+by one divfinal; its only built-in literal is zero. Generated plans use precisely
+this native schema. Bind copies and flag refs are also remapped during SSA expansion.
+
+## Offline SSA representation
+
+`compile_expression` and `compile_program` retain a development IR before encoding:
+
+```json
+{
+  "format": "tensorfold.runner.graph-plan",
+  "version": 1,
+  "literals": [{"digits": [7], "sign": 1, "error": 0}],
+  "nodes": [{"op": "add", "a": {"literal": 0}, "b": {"literal": 0}, "width": 2}],
+  "rootref": {"node": 0}
+}
+```
+
+Digits are little-endian decimal lanes, sign is 1 for negative, and error is sticky.
+Each reference has exactly one key: `literal` indexes the literal binding table and
+`node` indexes a previous call's result. All nodes have exactly `op`, `a`, `b`, `width`.
+Operations are `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `div` (Python floor division), and `mod`.
+Powers are unrolled into multiply calls using exponentiation by squaring. Loops, sums,
+list literals and comprehensions become fixed call sequences; no arithmetic answers
+are folded. Widths follow syntactic upper bounds, capped at the 62-digit register limit.
+Before a call, zero-extend shorter inputs to its width. Never truncate nonzero high
+lanes silently: truncation makes the input error sticky. Zero signs are normalized.
+
+## Native sequencing
+
+`div` and `mod` select a fixed width-specific division plan. Initialize unsigned Q and
+R to zero. For every dividend digit from high to low, bind `(R, abs(B), nextdigit)` to
+the precompiled `divstep` graph. Move output 0 directly to R; insert output 1's digit 0
+into that iteration's fixed quotient position. After exactly width steps, bind
+`(Q, R, original A, original B)` to `divfinal`. Its outputs are signed floor quotient
+and remainder; `div` selects output 0 and `mod` selects output 1. Metadata selects
+lanes; arithmetic and zero/sign decisions execute in FFNs. No text roundtrip is used.
+
+`divstep` shifts the remainder into width+1 lanes, performs nine guarded unsigned
+subtractions, and emits an unsigned remainder and quotient digit. `divfinal` corrects
+opposite signs with nonzero remainder using `|Q|+1` and `|B|-R`, normalizes zero signs,
+and propagates input errors and divisor-zero errors to both results.
+
+`native_packet(plan)` lowers the development IR to the native inline codec, expanding
+div/mod into tensor transfers and divstep/divfinal calls. Generic SSA requests carry
+the data-only invocation sequence, including offline unrolled T5 bodies, and use the
+same preloaded FFN kernels. Validate all sizes, digit ranges, flags,
+widths and backward references before binding. Python parsing is offline fixture tooling.
+
+## Corpus and verification handoff
+
+The CLI reads the original `goldens-10000/cases.jsonl.gz` and manifest, routes every
+row before examining outputs, and retains all routable requests plus the first 20
+samples in original order. It routes only
+integer add/sub/mul/floor-div/mod/pow syntax, including mixed expressions. Fractions,
+decimal syntax and gcd abstain; the original loop-squares fixture has a fixed plan.
+Baseline `outcome` including `machine_limit`, exact machine output bytes, mathematical
+expected output, and exit code are copied unchanged. Reference execution remains the
+parent's job using Qwenputer's `calc.machine` and register limits. This tool never uses
+Python `eval`, `calc.expected`, or host bignums to compute answers. The corpus retains
+the original manifest's upstream MIT credit and full license text.
+
+Corpus entries have two execution modes, determined from syntax before reading any
+reference outcome: `named` for simple signed binary operations and the known loop,
+and `generic_ssa` for compound expressions. Their `request` contains respectively a
+named operand-only packet or a generic inline SSA packet. Generic entries have no
+`named_plan`; no corpus-ID plan or benchmark-specific plan enters the production bank.
+The catalog contains only general binary, exponent and bounded loop plans.
+
+Legacy compatibility is separate: `legacy_backend` is `calc` for every compound
+expression and every unsupported source, by structural policy independent of answers.
+Thus generic SSA feature checks cannot claim legacy token/output parity when the old
+machine reports a complexity limit. Use the original calc fallback for those legacy
+checks and count it. Named entries select `graph`; their exact original outputs still
+require comparison. `mode_counts`, `legacy_backend_counts`, `baseline_machine_limit_cases`
+and `machine_limit_by_mode` report these populations, including unsupported rows.
+`machine_limit_cases` counts the limits among graph-routable entries. A generic result
+matching the mathematical expected output does not establish a match to `final_output`.
+
+Example parent commands: `python3 tools/runner_graph_plans.py --catalog --output plans.json`
+and `python3 tools/runner_graph_plans.py --corpus PATH/goldens-10000 --samples 20 --output corpus.json`.
+
+Verification and integration limits are recorded in `runner-graph-results.md`.
diff --git a/tools/runner-graph-probe.zig b/tools/runner-graph-probe.zig
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..259870e1b1bced4e3f6b985218bd3d85375b299c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/runner-graph-probe.zig
@@ -0,0 +1,397 @@
+//! Native graph evidence: evaluator tokens, exact stdout, prepared-bank boot and backend lifecycle.
+const std = @import("std");
+const graph = @import("runner_graph.zig");
+const api = @import("runner_api.zig");
+const Allocator = std.mem.Allocator;
+const Hash = std.crypto.hash.sha2.Sha256;
+const byte_base: u32 = 3 * 32768 + 4 + 2 * 65536;
+const halt: u32 = byte_base + 512 + 8 + 16 + 16 + 128 + 256 + 5;
+
+const Case = struct {
+    id: []const u8,
+    packet: std.json.Value,
+    expected_output: []const u8,
+    expected_status: []const u8 = "halted",
+    expect_mismatch: bool = false,
+};
+
+const Row = struct {
+    id: []const u8,
+    pass: bool = false,
+    status: []const u8 = "not_started",
+    reason: []const u8 = "",
+    steps: u64 = 0,
+    raw_tokens: usize = 0,
+    alu_halts: usize = 0,
+    trace_valid: bool = false,
+    output_equal: bool = false,
+    detected_mismatch: bool = false,
+    machine_boot_ns: u64 = 0,
+    run_ns: u64 = 0,
+    cpu_ns: u64 = 0,
+    actual_output: []const u8 = "",
+    actual_canonical_sha256: []const u8 = "",
+    expected_canonical_sha256: []const u8 = "",
+    raw_trace_sha256: []const u8 = "",
+};
+
+const Seed = struct { packet: []const u8, output: []const u8, op: []const u8 };
+const Lifecycle = struct { pass: bool = false, checks: usize = 0, error_name: []const u8 = "not_requested" };
+const Options = struct {
+    manifest: []const u8,
+    cases: []const u8,
+    start: usize = 0,
+    count: usize = std.math.maxInt(usize),
+    budget: u64 = 100000,
+    lifecycle: bool = false,
+};
+const Report = struct {
+    pass: bool,
+    boot_wall_ns: u64,
+    boot_process_cpu_ns: u64,
+    run_wall_ns: u64,
+    run_process_cpu_ns: u64,
+    case_count: usize,
+    failed_cases: usize,
+    named_requests: usize,
+    generic_requests: usize,
+    steps: u64,
+    request_compiled_graphs: u64 = 0,
+    actual_canonical_sha256: []const u8,
+    raw_audit_trace_sha256: []const u8,
+    trace_encoding: []const u8 = "LEu32; corpus order; generated tokens only; GO excluded",
+    projection: []const u8 = "actual BYTE tokens and actual final HALT; internal ALU HALTs excluded",
+    compilation_evidence: []const u8 = "Bank.load prepared packs once; no Circuit.load or compiler calls",
+    lifecycle: Lifecycle,
+    cases: []const Row,
+};
+
+fn now() u64 {
+    var ts: std.c.timespec = undefined;
+    _ = std.c.clock_gettime(.MONOTONIC, &ts);
+    return @as(u64, @intCast(ts.sec)) * std.time.ns_per_s + @as(u64, @intCast(ts.nsec));
+}
+
+fn cpuNow() u64 {
+    var ts: std.c.timespec = undefined;
+    _ = std.c.clock_gettime(.PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID, &ts);
+    return @as(u64, @intCast(ts.sec)) * std.time.ns_per_s + @as(u64, @intCast(ts.nsec));
+}
+
+fn tokenHash(h: *Hash, token: u32) void {
+    var bytes: [4]u8 = undefined;
+    std.mem.writeInt(u32, &bytes, token, .little);
+    h.update(&bytes);
+}
+
+fn hex(a: Allocator, h: *Hash) ![]const u8 {
+    const bytes = std.fmt.bytesToHex(h.finalResult(), .lower);
+    return a.dupe(u8, &bytes);
+}
+
+fn expectedHash(a: Allocator, bytes: []const u8, halted: bool) ![]const u8 {
+    var h = Hash.init(.{});
+    for (bytes) |b| tokenHash(&h, byte_base + b);
+    if (halted) tokenHash(&h, halt);
+    return hex(a, &h);
+}
+
+fn options(args: []const []const u8) !Options {
+    if (args.len < 3) return error.ExpectedManifestAndCases;
+    var o: Options = .{ .manifest = args[1], .cases = args[2] };
+    var i: usize = 3;
+    while (i < args.len) : (i += 1) {
+        if (std.mem.eql(u8, args[i], "--lifecycle")) {
+            o.lifecycle = true;
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (i + 1 >= args.len) return error.MissingOptionValue;
+        const key = args[i];
+        i += 1;
+        if (std.mem.eql(u8, key, "--start")) {
+            o.start = try std.fmt.parseInt(usize, args[i], 10);
+        } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, key, "--count") or std.mem.eql(u8, key, "--maxcases")) {
+            o.count = try std.fmt.parseInt(usize, args[i], 10);
+        } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, key, "--budget")) {
+            o.budget = try std.fmt.parseInt(u64, args[i], 10);
+        } else return error.UnknownOption;
+    }
+    return o;
+}
+
+fn canonicalBank(bank: *const graph.Bank) !void {
+    for (bank.templates) |t| {
+        if (t.circuit.halt != halt or t.circuit.byte_family != 6) return error.NoncanonicalBank;
+        const family, const payload = t.circuit.split(byte_base + 255) orelse return error.NoncanonicalBank;
+        if (family != 6 or payload != 255) return error.NoncanonicalBank;
+    }
+}
+
+fn audit(a: Allocator, row: *Row, trace: []const u32, out: []const u8, halted: bool, all_raw: *Hash, all_visible: *Hash) !void {
+    var raw = Hash.init(.{});
+    var visible = Hash.init(.{});
+    var valid = trace.len == row.steps;
+    var cursor: usize = 0;
+    for (trace, 0..) |token, i| {
+        tokenHash(&raw, token);
+        tokenHash(all_raw, token);
+        const is_byte = token >= byte_base and token < byte_base + 256;
+        if (is_byte) {
+            if (i < row.alu_halts or cursor >= out.len) {
+                valid = false;
+            } else if (token != byte_base + out[cursor]) valid = false;
+            cursor += 1;
+            tokenHash(&visible, token);
+            tokenHash(all_visible, token);
+        } else {
+            if (token != halt) valid = false;
+            if (halted and i + 1 == trace.len) {
+                tokenHash(&visible, token);
+                tokenHash(all_visible, token);
+            } else if (i >= row.alu_halts) valid = false;
+        }
+    }
+    if (cursor != out.len) valid = false;
+    if (halted) {
+        if (trace.len != row.alu_halts + out.len + 1) valid = false;
+        if (trace.len == 0 or trace[trace.len - 1] != halt) valid = false;
+    }
+    row.trace_valid = valid;
+    row.raw_tokens = trace.len;
+    row.actual_canonical_sha256 = try hex(a, &visible);
+    row.raw_trace_sha256 = try hex(a, &raw);
+}
+
+fn runCase(a: Allocator, keep: Allocator, bank: *const graph.Bank, c: Case, budget: u64, all_raw: *Hash, all_visible: *Hash, seeds: *std.ArrayList(Seed)) !Row {
+    var row: Row = .{ .id = try keep.dupe(u8, c.id) };
+    row.expected_canonical_sha256 = try expectedHash(keep, c.expected_output, std.mem.eql(u8, c.expected_status, "halted"));
+    const bytes = try std.json.Stringify.valueAlloc(a, c.packet, .{});
+    defer a.free(bytes);
+    const boot_start = now();
+    var m = graph.Machine.boot(a, bank, bytes) catch |err| {
+        row.machine_boot_ns = now() - boot_start;
+        row.status = try std.fmt.allocPrint(keep, "error:{s}", .{@errorName(err)});
+        row.pass = !c.expect_mismatch and std.mem.eql(u8, row.status, c.expected_status) and
+            c.expected_output.len == 0;
+        if (!row.pass) row.reason = "machine boot status differs";
+        return row;
+    };
+    defer m.deinit();
+    row.machine_boot_ns = now() - boot_start;
+    if (m.ops.len > 4096) {
+        row.reason = "case exceeds 4096 operation limit";
+        return row;
+    }
+    for (m.ops) |op| if (!std.mem.eql(u8, op.op, "bind")) {
+        row.alu_halts += 1;
+    };
+    var trace: std.ArrayList(u32) = .empty;
+    defer trace.deinit(a);
+    m.trace = &trace;
+    var out: std.ArrayList(u8) = .empty;
+    defer out.deinit(a);
+    const start = now();
+    const cpu_start = cpuNow();
+    const end: ?api.RunEnd = m.run(budget, &out, null) catch |err| blk: {
+        row.status = try std.fmt.allocPrint(keep, "error:{s}", .{@errorName(err)});
+        break :blk null;
+    };
+    row.cpu_ns = cpuNow() - cpu_start;
+    row.run_ns = now() - start;
+    row.steps = m.steps;
+    if (end) |e| row.status = @tagName(e.end);
+    const halted = std.mem.eql(u8, row.status, "halted");
+    try audit(keep, &row, trace.items, out.items, halted, all_raw, all_visible);
+    row.actual_output = try keep.dupe(u8, out.items);
+    row.output_equal = std.mem.eql(u8, out.items, c.expected_output);
+    row.detected_mismatch = halted and row.trace_valid and !row.output_equal;
+    row.pass = if (c.expect_mismatch) row.detected_mismatch else row.trace_valid and row.output_equal and std.mem.eql(u8, row.status, c.expected_status);
+    if (!row.pass) row.reason = "status, output or generated token trace differs";
+    if (row.pass and halted and !c.expect_mismatch and seeds.items.len < 2) {
+        const op = if (m.ops.len > 0) m.ops[0].op else "identity";
+        if (seeds.items.len == 0 or !std.mem.eql(u8, op, seeds.items[0].op)) {
+            try seeds.append(keep, .{ .packet = try keep.dupe(u8, bytes), .output = row.actual_output, .op = try keep.dupe(u8, op) });
+        }
+    }
+    return row;
+}
+
+fn wait(b: api.Backend, id: api.JobId) !api.Result {
+    const until = now() + 300 * std.time.ns_per_s;
+    while (true) {
+        switch (b.poll(id)) {
+            .done => |r| return r,
+            .running => {},
+        }
+        if (now() >= until) return error.BackendTimeout;
+        const delay: std.c.timespec = .{ .sec = 0, .nsec = std.time.ns_per_ms };
+        _ = std.c.nanosleep(&delay, null);
+    }
+}
+
+fn require(ok: bool) !void {
+    if (!ok) return error.BackendContract;
+}
+
+fn result(b: api.Backend, job: api.JobId, want: []const u8) !void {
+    const r = try wait(b, job);
+    try require(r.status == .ok and std.mem.eql(u8, r.out, want));
+    try require(r.steps > 0);
+}
+
+fn retryStart(b: api.Backend, stream: u64, program: api.Program, budget: u64) !api.JobId {
+    const until = now() + 300 * std.time.ns_per_s;
+    while (true) {
+        return b.start(stream, program, budget) catch |err| {
+            if (err != error.Busy) return err;
+            if (now() >= until) return error.BackendTimeout;
+            const delay: std.c.timespec = .{ .sec = 0, .nsec = std.time.ns_per_ms };
+            _ = std.c.nanosleep(&delay, null);
+            continue;
+        };
+    }
+}
+
+fn lifecycle(a: Allocator, bank: *const graph.Bank, seeds: []const Seed, budget: u64, checks: *usize) !void {
+    const Kind = @FieldType(api.Program, "kind");
+    if (comptime !@hasField(Kind, "graph")) return error.GraphKindUnavailable;
+    const kind = std.meta.stringToEnum(Kind, "graph") orelse return error.GraphKindUnavailable;
+    if (seeds.len != 2) return error.NeedTwoDistinctOperations;
+    const p: api.Program = .{ .kind = kind, .bytes = seeds[0].packet };
+    const q: api.Program = .{ .kind = kind, .bytes = seeds[1].packet };
+    const b = try graph.backend(a, bank, 2);
+    defer graph.destroy(b);
+    const one = try b.start(1, p, budget);
+    const two = try b.start(2, q, budget);
+    if (b.start(3, p, budget)) |_| return error.MissingBusy else |err| try require(err == error.Busy);
+    checks.* += 1;
+    try result(b, two, seeds[1].output);
+    try result(b, one, seeds[0].output);
+    checks.* += 1;
+    switch (b.poll(one)) {
+        .running => return error.DeliveredTwice,
+        .done => |r| try require(r.status == .abstain and r.out.len == 0),
+    }
+    checks.* += 1;
+    const zero = try b.start(1, p, 0);
+    const limited = try wait(b, zero);
+    try require(limited.status == .budget and limited.steps == 0 and limited.out.len == 0);
+    checks.* += 1;
+    try result(b, try b.start(1, p, budget), seeds[0].output);
+    checks.* += 1;
+    const cancelled = try b.start(4, p, budget);
+    b.cancel(cancelled);
+    try result(b, try retryStart(b, 4, q, budget), seeds[1].output);
+    checks.* += 1;
+    _ = try b.start(5, q, budget);
+    b.release(5);
+    try result(b, try retryStart(b, 5, p, budget), seeds[0].output);
+    checks.* += 1;
+    b.release(1);
+    b.release(2);
+    b.release(4);
+    b.release(5);
+    try result(b, try b.start(1, q, budget), seeds[1].output);
+    checks.* += 1;
+    var m = try graph.Machine.boot(a, bank, seeds[0].packet);
+    defer m.deinit();
+    var out: std.ArrayList(u8) = .empty;
+    defer out.deinit(a);
+    const flag = std.atomic.Value(bool).init(true);
+    const end = try m.run(budget, &out, &flag);
+    try require(end.end == .cancelled and m.steps == 0 and out.items.len == 0);
+    checks.* += 1;
+}
+
+fn run(init: std.process.Init) !u8 {
+    const a = init.gpa;
+    const keep = init.arena.allocator();
+    const args = try init.minimal.args.toSlice(keep);
+    const o = try options(args);
+    const boot_start = now();
+    const boot_cpu_start = cpuNow();
+    var bank = try graph.Bank.load(a, o.manifest);
+    const boot_cpu_ns = cpuNow() - boot_cpu_start;
+    const boot_ns = now() - boot_start;
+    defer bank.deinit();
+    try canonicalBank(&bank);
+    const bytes = try std.Io.Dir.cwd().readFileAlloc(init.io, o.cases, a, .limited(128 << 20));
+    defer a.free(bytes);
+    var lines = std.mem.splitScalar(u8, bytes, '\n');
+    var rows: std.ArrayList(Row) = .empty;
+    var seeds: std.ArrayList(Seed) = .empty;
+    var raw = Hash.init(.{});
+    var visible = Hash.init(.{});
+    var index: usize = 0;
+    var failed: usize = 0;
+    var named: usize = 0;
+    var generic: usize = 0;
+    var steps: u64 = 0;
+    const start = now();
+    const cpu_start = cpuNow();
+    while (lines.next()) |line| {
+        if (std.mem.trim(u8, line, "\r\t ").len == 0) continue;
+        const current = index;
+        index += 1;
+        if (current < o.start) continue;
+        if (rows.items.len >= o.count) break;
+        const parsed = std.json.parseFromSlice(Case, a, line, .{ .ignore_unknown_fields = true }) catch |err| {
+            const row: Row = .{ .id = try std.fmt.allocPrint(keep, "line-{d}", .{current + 1}), .reason = try keep.dupe(u8, @errorName(err)) };
+            try rows.append(keep, row);
+            failed += 1;
+            continue;
+        };
+        defer parsed.deinit();
+        const c = parsed.value;
+        if (c.packet == .object and c.packet.object.get("plan") != null) named += 1 else generic += 1;
+        const row = try runCase(a, keep, &bank, c, o.budget, &raw, &visible, &seeds);
+        try rows.append(keep, row);
+        if (!row.pass) failed += 1;
+        steps += row.steps;
+        if (rows.items.len % 100 == 0) std.debug.print("graph probe: {d} cases, {d} failures\n", .{
+            rows.items.len, failed,
+        });
+    }
+    const run_ns = now() - start;
+    const cpu_ns = cpuNow() - cpu_start;
+    var life: Lifecycle = .{};
+    if (o.lifecycle) {
+        life.error_name = "";
+        lifecycle(a, &bank, seeds.items, o.budget, &life.checks) catch |err| {
+            life.error_name = @errorName(err);
+        };
+        life.pass = life.error_name.len == 0 and life.checks == 9;
+    }
+    const report: Report = .{
+        .pass = rows.items.len > 0 and failed == 0 and (!o.lifecycle or life.pass),
+        .boot_wall_ns = boot_ns,
+        .boot_process_cpu_ns = boot_cpu_ns,
+        .run_wall_ns = run_ns,
+        .run_process_cpu_ns = cpu_ns,
+        .case_count = rows.items.len,
+        .failed_cases = failed,
+        .named_requests = named,
+        .generic_requests = generic,
+        .steps = steps,
+        .actual_canonical_sha256 = try hex(keep, &visible),
+        .raw_audit_trace_sha256 = try hex(keep, &raw),
+        .lifecycle = life,
+        .cases = rows.items,
+    };
+    const json = try std.json.Stringify.valueAlloc(keep, report, .{});
+    try std.Io.File.stdout().writeStreamingAll(init.io, json);
+    try std.Io.File.stdout().writeStreamingAll(init.io, "\n");
+    return if (report.pass) 0 else 1;
+}
+
+pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !u8 {
+    return run(init) catch |err| {
+        const json = try std.json.Stringify.valueAlloc(init.arena.allocator(), .{
+            .pass = false,
+            .fatal_error = @errorName(err),
+        }, .{});
+        try std.Io.File.stdout().writeStreamingAll(init.io, json);
+        try std.Io.File.stdout().writeStreamingAll(init.io, "\n");
+        return 1;
+    };
+}
